{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.DilogPartBAEFinal","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DilogPartBAEFinal","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.DilogPartBAEAssembly","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.DilogPartBWindowMeasure"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ae_bdry_tendsto_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ae_bdry_tendsto_zero","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/DilogPartBAEFinal.lean#L109-L125","doc":"**A.e. Borel–Cantelli assembly — the dilog Part-B W-P1 a.e. positive.**  For a.e.\n`x ∈ (0,1)`, along the Faddeev schedule `q_m = 1 + 1/(m+1)` the branch-index boundary term\n`(q_m − 1)·(−log(1 − x·q_m^{⌊s_m⌋})) → 0`.  Borel–Cantelli (`ae_eventually_notMem` +\n`tsum_volume_resWindow_ne_top`) gives a.e. eventual no-resonance\n(`ε_m ≤ frac(s_m)`), which the squeeze `bdry_tendsto_of_eventually_no_resonance` turns into\nconvergence.  This is the measure-theoretic positive complementing the proved-false\nunconditional pointwise limit (`not_tendsto_boundary_zero`, #4434). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.tsum_volume_resWindow_ne_top","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.tsum_volume_resWindow_ne_top","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/DilogPartBAEFinal.lean#L98-L107","doc":"**Summable window measure** `Σ_m volume(W_m) ≠ ∞`.  From `volume_resWindow_le` +\n`epsBC_summable` (the p-series). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.volume_resWindow_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.volume_resWindow_le","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/DilogPartBAEFinal.lean#L71-L96","doc":"**Window measure bound** `volume(W_m) ≤ 2·ε_m`.  From `volume_window_le_geom`\n(`≤ (1−q^{−ε})q/(q−1)`) and `(1−q^{−ε})q/(q−1) ≤ ε·log q·q/(q−1) ≤ ε·q ≤ 2ε` (using\n`1−q^{−ε} ≤ ε log q`, `log q ≤ q−1`, `q ≤ 2`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.resWindow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.resWindow","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/DilogPartBAEFinal.lean#L67-L69","doc":"The resonance window at step `m`: `W_m = {x ∈ (0,1) : frac(s_m) < ε_m}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.bdry_tendsto_of_eventually_no_resonance","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.bdry_tendsto_of_eventually_no_resonance","kind":"theorem","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/DilogPartBAEFinal.lean#L34-L65","doc":"**Analytic squeeze — eventual no-resonance ⇒ boundary term vanishes.**  For `x ∈ (0,1)`, if\n`ε_m ≤ frac(s_m)` eventually (the no-resonance condition), the branch-index boundary term\n`(q_m − 1)·(−log(1 − x·q_m^{⌊s_m⌋})) → 0`.  It is squeezed between `0` (from `q_m > 1` and\n`0 < δ_m ≤ 1`) and the vanishing majorant `(q_m−1)·(−log((ε_m/4)(q_m−1)))`\n(`tendsto_boundary_majorant`), using `branch_gap_lower_of_fract` for `δ_m ≥ (ε_m/4)(q_m−1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.epsBC_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.epsBC_pos","kind":"theorem","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/DilogPartBAEFinal.lean#L32-L32","signatureChunk":0}]}